<circuit version="1.1.0-SR2" rev="261104" stepSize="1000000" stepsPS="1000000" NLsteps="100000" reaStep="1000000" animate="0" >
<description>
# 2N3819 amplifier as published (jotrin.com / components101)

VCC 12 V, R1 100k / R2 10k gate divider, RC 10k, source grounded, C1 = C2 = 1 uF; 1 kHz, 100 mV p-p in, RL 100k on the output. Q1 is SimulIDE's JFET, Model 2N3819.

It does not amplify [SIMULATED]: the divider puts +1.09 V on the gate of an N-channel JFET whose source is grounded. The gate junction is forward biased (gate clamped at 0.55 V, 53 uA into the gate), the channel is fully on (OHMIC) and the drain sits at 0.13 V. 100 mV p-p in gives 3.5 mV out: gain 0.035.

A JFET's gate must be negative of its source: see amp_self_bias_duncan.sim1 (the textbook circuit) and amp_source_resistor.sim1 (this circuit plus a source resistor).
</description>


